            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski Hit this as well multiple times in various hard-to-reproduce circumstances.\r\n\r\nJust a thought, maybe the problem's this:\r\n- you're in a situation where `:bnext` and `:bprev` don't do anything (i.e `:buffers` is empty)\r\n- but `b#` does switch back to the alternate buffer\r\n- this occurs sometimes when in lazyvim you restore session (e.g. when editing the nvim config itself and then restarting nvim) and immediately `gd` (go to lsp definition) somewhere and then try to close it via `.delete(0, true/false)`.\r\n\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua: ...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:143: Error executing lua: vim/_editor.lua:0: nvim_exec2(): Vim(bprevious):E85: There is no listed buffer\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_exec2'\r\n\tvim/_editor.lua: in function 'cmd'\r\n\t...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:157: in function <...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:143>\r\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_win_call'\r\n\t...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:143: in function <...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:133>\r\n\tvim/shared.lua: in function 'tbl_map'\r\n\t...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:119: in function 'unshow'\r\n\t...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:216: in function 'delete'\r\n\t...l/share/nvim/lazy/LazyVim/lua/lazyvim/plugins/editor.lua:339: in function <...l/share/nvim/lazy/LazyVim/lua/lazyvim/plugins/editor.lua:339>\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_win_call'\r\n\t...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:143: in function <...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:133>\r\n\tvim/shared.lua: in function 'tbl_map'\r\n\t...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:119: in function 'unshow'\r\n\t...al/share/nvim/lazy/mini.bufremove/lua/mini/bufremove.lua:216: in function 'delete'\r\n```"