            "body": "> @echasnovski Thanks for the prompt reply. Tbh I have no prior experience in creating reproducible examples in nvim, any tips on how to try to isolate it? (i.e. creating a working minimal environment with bufremove and perhaps a few other plugins that may interfere?)\r\n\r\nSure.\r\n- Put (via `git clone`, for example) necessary  plugins somewhere where you can load them. I suggest 'pack/plugins/opt/' directory inside your config ('\\~/.config/nvim' in Unix). For example, you should have '~/.config/nvim/pack/plugins/opt/mini.nvim' with latest code changes (or 'mini.bufremove' if you want to clone standalone repository).\r\n- Create 'repro-init.lua' file (or any other name). It should load and initialize plugins. Following previous step, it should contain at least something like this:\r\n```lua\r\n-- Make Neovim aware about 'mini.nvim' source code\r\nvim.cmd('packadd mini.nvim')\r\n\r\n-- Initialize 'mini.bufremove'\r\nrequire('mini.bufremove').setup()\r\n\r\n-- Some other initialization you wish to do on startup\r\n```\r\n\r\n- Start neovim with `nvim --noplugin -u repro-init.lua`.\r\n- Perform actions which lead to the error. Make sure that they consistently lead to the same error.\r\n- Put your 'repro-init.lua' file and steps: either here or in a new issue.\r\n\r\nNote, that if error can be reproduced only with another plugin, then it also might be the reason of the error.",
